ces and support limits, then uses strict separation. The terminal retains both inclusions and has no supplied witness, closed-hull replacement, global finiteness, bounded-domain or component closedness assumption.\n\nThis PR stacks on OPEN draft #172 at exact bd70b48eaff11accad19e5009efbdce3efd4b8c5. Seventeen retained proofs (one numbered terminal and sixteen foundations) and two complete retained definitions are source-qualified; no mathematical, TEST or registry declaration is added. The ordinary leading scope comment preserves every original raw mathematical byte. All nineteen headers, the complete old canary, shared roots/toolchain/dependencies and every other Book are preserved. Source: arXiv:1912.13213v10, printed18/PDF30, SHA256 cef4edfa97a6e063e53e9c532717c50aa156e5bc782ea49f969b3385011a1b17.\n\nDistinct required formalizer, restricted decoder and anti-anchored reviewer completed CONTRACT/BODY/FINAL with explicit semantic deltas. These are automated roles, not human/external review or attested runtime model provenance. The maximum definition needs only an arbitrary ambient type and finite nonempty indexing; the active union has intrinsic real inner-product structure. Actual theorem/helper premises remain individually explicit. The shared global support predicate permits improper EReal inputs, while this source terminal supplies proper components and a common domain query. Positive infinity away from that query is permitted. The finite-dimensional inner-product formulation includes Euclidean instances; no separately certified coordinate conversion, algorithm, regret or measurable selection guarantee is claimed.\n\nCurrent root 9089 jobs, Tests 9234 jobs and full harness 466 tests / 7 existing skips pass (cached jobs included). All nineteen old canary proofs and two TEST definitions, forty unique standard-foundation kernel checks and nineteen native header guards pass. The scalar canary checks fractional hull membership, a strict active component and an exten